[metadata] {"type": "create", "filePath": "/app/output/final_report.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Nine Decades of Oscar-Winning Scores (1934–2026)</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --gold: #C9A84C;
    --gold-light: #F0D080;
    --gold-dark: #8B6914;
    --bg-dark: #0D0D0F;
    --bg-card: #16161A;
    --bg-card2: #1E1E24;
    --text-primary: #F0EDE8;
    --text-secondary: #A89F8C;
    --text-muted: #6B6560;
    --accent-blue: #4A90C4;
    --accent-red: #C45A4A;
    --accent-green: #5AAF6E;
    --border: rgba(201,168,76,0.2);
    --border-subtle: rgba(255,255,255,0.07);
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

  body {
    font-family: 'Georgia', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    background: var(--bg-dark);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  /* ── HEADER ── */
  .report-header {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1A1508 0%, var(--bg-dark) 100%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 64px 0 48px;
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .report-header::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 60% at 50% -10%, rgba(201,168,76,0.12), transparent);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .oscar-icon {
    font-size: 48px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    display: block;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 12px rgba(201,168,76,0.5));
  }
  .report-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .report-header .subtitle {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .report-header .one-liner {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── LAYOUT ── */
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px; }
  .section { padding: 60px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }
  .section:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .section-label {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    display: block;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding-left: 16px;
  }
  .section-body {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .section-body p { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .section-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  strong { color: var(--text-primary); }

  /* ── KPI CARDS ── */
  .kpi-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 32px 0;
  }
  .kpi-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 28px 24px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .kpi-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gold-dark), var(--gold-light), var(--gold-dark));
  }
  .kpi-card:hover { border-color: rgba(201,168,76,0.4); }
  .kpi-value {
    font-size: 42px;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .kpi-label {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .kpi-context {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── BAR CHARTS ── */
  .bar-chart { margin: 0; }
  .bar-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .bar-name {
    width: 220px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-align: right;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .bar-track {
    flex: 1;
    height: 28px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
  }
  .bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding-left: 8px;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgba(0,0,0,0.7);
    transition: width 0.6s ease;
    min-width: 28px;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .bar-wins {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    width: 32px;
    text-align: right;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .bar-years {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .bar-top { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #C9A84C, #F0D080); }
  .bar-high { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #A8894A, #C9A84C); }
  .bar-mid { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #6B5835, #957840); }
  .bar-low { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #3A3020, #6B5835); }

  /* ── DECADE TABLE ── */
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .data-table th {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    padding: 12px 16px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }
  .data-table td {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .data-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .data-table tr:hover td { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); }
  .data-table td:first-child {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .decade-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--bg-card2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-right: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }

  /* ── ERA CARDS ── */
  .era-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }
  .era-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 24px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .era-card::after {
    content: attr(data-era);
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -8px; right: -4px;
    font-size: 64px;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
    line-height: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .era-name {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .era-years {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .era-stat { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 13px; }
  .era-stat-label { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .era-stat-value { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; }
  .era-desc { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-top: 14px; font-style: italic; }

  /* ── MILESTONES TIMELINE ── */
  .timeline { position: relative; padding-left: 32px; }
  .timeline::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; left: 8px; top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--gold), var(--gold-dark), transparent);
  }
  .timeline-item {
    position: relative;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 8px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .timeline-item:hover { border-color: var(--border); }
  .timeline-item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute; left: -28px; top: 22px;
    width: 10px; height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--gold);
    border: 2px solid var(--bg-dark);
    box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(201,168,76,0.4);
  }
  .milestone-year {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .milestone-title { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .milestone-body { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); }

  /* ── STREAK CARDS ── */
  .streak-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  .streak-card {
    background: var(--bg-card2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .streak-card.highlight { border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card); }
  .streak-composer { font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .streak-years { font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 22px; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .streak-films { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); font-style: italic; }

  /* ── CONCLUSIONS ── */
  .takeaway-list { list-style: none; }
  .takeaway-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .takeaway-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .takeaway-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 36px; height: 36px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--gold-dark), var(--gold));
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #000;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .takeaway-text strong { display: block; font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .takeaway-text p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); }

  /* ── SVG CHARTS ── */
  .chart-container { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 10px; padding: 24px; margin: 24px 0; }
  .chart-title {
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  svg text { font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif; }

  /* ── FOOTER ── */
  .report-footer {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 32px 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .report-footer a { color: var(--gold); text-decoration: none; }

  /* ── UTILITY ── */
  .highlight-text { color: var(--gold-light); }
  .mt-8 { margin-top: 8px; }
  .mt-16 { margin-top: 16px; }
  .mt-24 { margin-top: 24px; }
  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(201,168,76,0.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(201,168,76,0.3);
    color: var(--gold);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .container { padding: 0 16px; }
    .bar-name { width: 130px; font-size: 12px; }
    .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .era-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════ HEADER -->
<header class="report-header">
  <span class="oscar-icon">🏆</span>
  <h1>Nine Decades of Oscar-Winning Scores</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Academy Award for Best Original Score &nbsp;·&nbsp; 1934 – 2026</p>
  <p class="one-liner">A historical trend analysis of all 93 ceremonies — tracking who dominated, how tastes shifted, and what the data reveals about film music's highest honor.</p>
</header>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════ SECTION 1: OVERVIEW -->
<div class="container">
<section class="section" id="overview">
  <span class="section-label">Section 01</span>
  <h2 class="section-title">Dataset Overview &amp; Historical Context</h2>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>The Academy Award for Best Original Score has been conferred without interruption since the <strong>6th Academy Awards ceremony in 1934</strong>, making it one of the oldest and most storied honors in cinema. This analysis draws on the complete record of <strong>93 ceremonies</strong> spanning from that inaugural year through the <strong>98th ceremony in 2026</strong> — a span wide enough to capture the full arc of Hollywood's relationship with orchestral drama, jazz fusion, electronic experimentation, and the globally inflected soundscapes of contemporary scoring.</p>
    <p>The dataset is compact but analytically rich: three columns — Year, Film, Composer — yield a precise ledger of the industry's collective judgment across nine decades. Across those 93 ceremonies, <strong>69 distinct composer entries</strong> took the award; when collaborative credits are decomposed into individual contributors, the total rises to approximately <strong>79 unique individuals</strong>. That gap — ten extra names — reflects the Academy's occasional recognition of multi-composer collaborations, a practice notably more common in the early era and again in the contemporary period.</p>
    <p>Historically, the category has not been static in its rules. The Academy occasionally split the award into sub-categories (dramatic vs. comedy/musical scores) and later consolidated back to a single winner. This dataset, consistent with academic convention, presents one consolidated winner per year, reflecting the prevailing Best Original Score determination for each ceremony.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- KPI CARDS -->
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">93</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Ceremonies</div>
      <div class="kpi-context">6th Academy Awards (1934) through 98th (2026)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">69</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Unique Composer Entries</div>
      <div class="kpi-context">Distinct credited entities; ~79 individual composers when collaborative groups are split</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">4</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Maximum Wins — Single Composer</div>
      <div class="kpi-context">Shared by John Barry, John Williams &amp; Ludwig Göransson</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">28%</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Repeat Winner Rate</div>
      <div class="kpi-context">26 of 93 ceremonies won by a previously awarded composer</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">1980s</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Decade with Most Unique Winners</div>
      <div class="kpi-context">10 ceremonies, 10 different composers — 100% unique rate</div>
    </div>
